From: TicWatch Pro 5 port
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: icc-rpm: stub RPM voting (dace bring-up)

The hard crash to EDL after the ICC nodes of qnoc-monaco register points at
RPM voting (icc_set_bw -> qcom_icc_rpm_set -> qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send). With this
stub the drivers get their paths (deferred resolved, eMMC alive) without
touching the RPM; the bus keeps the bootloader rates.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
---

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
index ffa1d16e0..6aff60c75 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
@@ -108,6 +108,14 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(qcom_icc_rpm_aggregate);
  */
 int qcom_icc_rpm_set(struct icc_node *src, struct icc_node *dst)
 {
+	/* dace bring-up: do not send votes to the RPM. The hard crash to EDL
+	 * after the ICC nodes of qnoc-monaco register points at RPM voting
+	 * (icc_set_bw -> qcom_icc_rpm_set -> qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send). With this
+	 * stub the drivers get their paths (deferred resolved, eMMC alive)
+	 * without touching the RPM; the bus keeps the rates the bootloader left
+	 * (enough for bring-up). Remove once RPM voting is debugged. */
+	return 0;
+#pragma message("dace: qcom_icc_rpm_set STUB (no RPM voting)")
 	struct qcom_icc_provider *qp;
 	struct qcom_icc_node *qn;
 	struct icc_node *n, *node;
